From 353db74d9e5bb4778f996bf4692d0f1a058fcf2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:22:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): warn on start-side stand-in entries and a Plunge
 into stock

A plain Outside pocket with no stock known has no air room, so the Arc
entry at a later pass start in material took a named ramp along the
pass, and a selected Plunge plunged into uncut stock. Both were notes
only. The op page dropped them, and no warning was posted.

- A start-side ladder marks each stand-in entry (ENTRY_STAND_IN_NOTE);
  the op posts one advisory Warning::EntryStandIn that counts them.
- A start-side pass link that plunges into a pass start in material
  writes PLUNGE_INTO_STOCK_NOTE; the op posts one advisory
  Warning::PlungeIntoStock (not when EntryNotRecommended names it).
- entry_status_lines shows each stand-in entry as a warning line.
- MCP names the two kinds entry_stand_in and plunge_into_stock.

Decision: docs/decisions/3884-start-side-entry-warnings.md.

Fixes #3884

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
